  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 3: REGROUP — THE CALM AND THE STORM"
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck was waiting in the Guild’s material vestibule, a place of solid stone and rushing geothermal waters."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "He was cleaning blood—dark, oily, not his own—from his claws."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "His report was terse."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "“The Orion remnant is a ghost town."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "But their docks are not empty."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "A slaver convoy, using old Sirian jump-ships."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "They are loading ‘cargo’ in the subterranean hangars."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "The cargo is alive."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "Terrified.”"
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh flowed from the shadows, her form coalescing. “I have been… listening."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "Through the network’s nascent connection here."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "The slavers are not just trading."
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "They have a contract."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "They are delivering workers to the asteroid belt."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "A mining operation of impossible scale.”"
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "“A mining operation,” Geralt repeated, the pieces clicking with dreadful synergy. “Pulling the fragments of the Shattered Mind back together.”"
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "“The slaves are the tools,” Oreck growled. “Human bridges."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "They link the fragments with crude gravity tethers."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "The mortality rate is the point."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "The dead are just… discarded mass.”"
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "The image was horrifying."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "It was slavery reduced to its most brutally literal form: using living bodies as literal glue to reassemble a dead god’s skull for a mad queen."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "“We need that shuttle,” Geralt said, the numb certainty of his training overriding the surge of rage. “It’s our ticket in, and it’s our first strike.”"
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "The Plan: A heist."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "Not a frontal assault."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "The slaver captain was known to be arrogant, greedy, and fond of gambling on pit-fights in the lower lunar taverns."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck would be the bait—a fearsome, exotic challenger."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh would be the shadow, infiltrating the ship’s systems."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt would be the anchor, applying causal inertia in tiny, crucial moments: a guard’s hesitation, a lock’s failure, a distracted glance at the wrong time."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "It was a messy, dangerous, physical job."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "The absolute opposite of cosmic time-weaving."
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "It was exactly what he needed."
  - line: 161
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

